Z||000000||Tabs||08-26-2001||02:46 PM||||I was think about buying some stuff over e-bay for my fiero and I was wonderin if anybody else has done the same and have they had any problems getting what they bid for??<P>PLus I live in Canada is there a Canadian E-bat by any chance<P>Tabs||||reg||1
Z||000001||hyhy4u||08-26-2001||02:55 PM||||Ive bought so much stuff online..mostly ebay in teh past couple years! Stuff for my fiero..stereo..just whatever..Only had a problem once.  As long as they have a credible rating and the price is right i would say go for it!||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||08-26-2001||02:55 PM||||I've had a few snags, but always ended up getting what I paid for.. same goes for a lot of people.. however, I know just as many people who have been burned by ebay sellers.. check out a person's feedback before you place any bids, if they're not a reliable seller, avoid them..<P>and yes, there is an ebay canada.. link is on the main ebay site.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000003||Cheever3000||08-26-2001||03:30 PM||||I've gotten a few things here & there, nothing real expensive however.  No problems yet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||mbramble||08-26-2001||03:32 PM||||I have bought a LOT of stuff off ebay from Fiero parts to PC components to audio stuff.  I have had a problem with only one person.  I did get my item but it was like pulling teeth.  He seemed to have started out good, had good feedback when I bid -- but at the same time I had a problem, many others did as well.  He finally got the boot.  Every other transaction has been painless.<P>Look at the person's feedback before bidding.  If he has any negatives with no good explanations posted, stay away. If he is new, correspond with him via e-mail and ask whatever questions you feel are relevant before bidding.<P>Watch out for the 'hidden' costs.  Shipping, handling, package, etc., costs.  Some roll all but the actual shipping into their minimum bids, others want to tack on the costs of buying a box, tape, etc., to the final bid plus the cost of shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000005||banditbalz||08-26-2001||04:00 PM||||Tabs, I have bought a tonne of stuff off ebay over the past year. Never had a problem. As far as a Canadian ebay goes, try this link... <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ebay.ca" TARGET=_blank>www.ebay.ca</A> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000006||PAUL88GT||08-26-2001||04:08 PM||||Generally speaking, you will pay more for used parts on e-bay.  You can do better by going to salvage yards if you have the time and inclination.  Much of what you are paying for on e-bay is the convenience of getting the part you need shipped directly to your front door which is worth something. You can also get good prices on parts at swap meets and from parts vendors at car shows. I have sold and bought several parts on e-bay without problems. I just kind of look at e-bay as the last resort for used Fiero parts.   A good low cost source of new GM parts is <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com." TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com.</A> <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spektrum-87GT||08-26-2001||06:17 PM||||i got my fiero off of ebay... well, sort of. I've always had positive experiences with ebay. Just wished shipping was a little quicker with some sellers.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fiero5||08-26-2001||06:27 PM||||I would say that going to Bob Parker at Kick Hill farms is even better than the salvage yards. It's a Fiero candy store there, with usually better quality stuff than what you can get "lucky" finding at the junk yards. A huge 3 story barn full of carefully removed used Fiero parts.<P>I love going there! Or call him and he can ship, and he doesn't charge stupid money to ship things either. None of this high shipping "and" handling charge crap like many of the e-bay sellers pull.<P>Having said that, I have gotten some cool stuff off e-bay, but not parts. Things like old Fiero mags, t-shirts, flyers, ads and stuff like that. I can do better with parts thru Kick Hill. Plus I don't have to waite a week, stay at the computer till the very last seconds to "try" and not get beat out and all that hastle.<P>Just my 2 penny's<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000009||Philphine||08-26-2001||07:42 PM||||i've gotten 2 cars, a bunch of sets of wheels, a couple guitars and other stuff off ebay no probs.<P>except outlaw   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>a man of constant sorrow||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||08-26-2001||08:21 PM||||I buy and sell a ton of stuff. Lisa sold some too. One persons junk is anothers prize. I just won a Pocher 1/8 scale diecast Testa Rossa. Should be here tommorro  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> If youve never seen them there huge almost 2' long. everything works on them, even tiny ignition keys for doors and steering column. Mines got real leather interior and carpeting. They even make floor mats and car covers for them. I already have a Porsche Carerra.||||reg||1
